    "narrations": {
      "w1-title": "Your heart beats about one hundred thousand times every single day. Today, we draw how it keeps you alive.",
      "w1-process": "Here is the loop. The right side pumps blood to the lungs to pick up oxygen. The left side then fires it out to the whole body.",
      "w1-comparison": "An athlete's resting heart beats about forty times a minute. The average heart sits near seventy. Training makes every beat count.",
      "w1-phrase": "If you remember one number, make it this one: sixty to one hundred beats every minute.",
      "w1-conclusion": "Now you can draw the heart yourself. Sketch it, label it, and share the story."
    }
  },
